[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://scenes/parts/KillFloor.tscn" id="killfloor"]

; A stepped bowl with high walls on both sides: each half is a staircase
; descending toward the middle, and the walls run from well above head height
; down past the lowest step, so there is no way out sideways at any height a
; fight happens at. The drain at the bottom centre (120 px) is floored by the
; DrainShelf (#1202) except a 30 px slot too narrow to fall through, so there
; is no ring-out: the Bowl is closed and damage decides the round.
;
; This is the one stage in the rotation where damage, not geometry, usually
; decides the round -- every other stage rewards putting someone over an edge,
; and there is barely an edge here. It exists so the rotation is not entirely a
; ring-out game, and so a player who is losing on health cannot simply run out
; of reach.
;
; Each half is one CollisionPolygon2D rather than a stack of separate step
; bodies, for the same reason Slant is: an earlier cut built the steps as four
; floating slabs and left 40 px of open air between each tier and the next, so
; the stage had three more ways out than its own description claimed. A single
; staircase polygon per side cannot develop a gap it was not drawn with.

; Backdrop (issue #117): purple dusk.
[node name="Bowl" type="Node2D"]
script = ExtResource("1")
background_sky_top = Color(0.12, 0.09, 0.2, 1)
background_sky_bottom = Color(0.26, 0.18, 0.26, 1)
background_silhouette = Color(0.12, 0.08, 0.14, 1)
background_layers = PackedStringArray("mountains", "hills")

